(742779, 51794, 7322, '<td valign="top">Not my favorite of your shots but it sure brings back memories of growing up in Swansea, Massachusetts. The area is full of these buggers. We used to have wars with them,to the ire of our parents who had to cut them out of our hair. The spikes get under your skin like fiberglass. Itchy!<br/> <br/>BTW, I love that you note the Latin name for them. We always just called them burrs and I''ve had a hard time describing them to people who haven''t experienced them. Now I know what to call them. <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-05-30 17:40:16.</i></td>', 'Not my favorite of your shots but it sure brings back memories of growing up in Swansea, Massachusetts. The area is full of these buggers. We used to have wars with them,to the ire of our parents who had to cut them out of our hair. The spikes get under your skin like fiberglass. Itchy! BTW, I love that you note the Latin name for them. We always just called them burrs and I''ve had a hard time describing them to people who haven''t experienced them. Now I know what to call them. ', '2004-05-30 18:38:29.000000', '2004-05-30 18:40:16.000000', 0),
